# src/html is EJS, not HTML. Prettier has no parser for .ejs and skips it on
# its own, but an editor or a plugin that maps .ejs to its html parser would
# not know `<%` from text - measured on the Nunjucks sources this kit used to
# ship, that rewrote 49 of 51 files and deleted every attribute inside a
# conditional, at exit code 0. Nothing formats a
# source template here - `npm run lint:fix:html` sorts the class VALUES in place
# and touches no other byte, and the formatter proper runs on dist/, which is
# pure HTML by then. This entry is what stops `npx prettier --write .` and
# format-on-save from doing it anyway.
#
# It does not affect the build: gulp-prettier calls prettier.format() directly
# and never reads this file, which is also why `dist` above costs nothing.
src/html
